sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant O as Orchestrator (code)
    participant P as Planner
    participant T as Tester
    participant C as Stage Coder
    participant SB as Sandbox MCP (Docker)
    participant V as Validator
    participant G as Git / Artifacts MCP
    participant W as Warehouse MCP

    U->>O: request, sources, expected result
    O->>O: load sources as text, profile (schema, stats, 5 sample rows)
    O->>P: request + source profiles
    P-->>O: PlanDraft (stages with input/output schemas)
    O->>O: validate plan (inputs exist, no cycles, names)
    O->>G: commit plan.json
    loop each stage in dependency order
        O->>T: stage spec + input profiles (no code)
        T-->>O: StageTests
        O->>C: stage spec + input schemas/samples
        C-->>O: StageCode
        Note over O,SB: inner build loop: see the second sequence diagram
        O->>G: commit stage code + tests, store versioned output
    end
    O->>V: output profiles + source profiles
    V-->>O: proposed rules
    O->>SB: run all rules (schema + request + derived) as code
    SB-->>O: CheckResults
    alt a check failed and quality rounds remain
        O->>C: re-code the producing stage with the failed checks
    else all checks pass, or rounds exhausted
        O->>W: stage_table + write_quarantine (production untouched)
        O-->>U: approval request (rows, quarantine, failed checks, preview)
        U->>O: approve or reject
        opt approved
            O->>W: promote(table, approval token bound to data fingerprint)
        end
        O->>G: commit manifest.json
        O-->>U: run report (plan, stages, retries, quality, rows, cost)
    end
